import Grail
-- Hdl, the hardware-description package (design: wiz-notes/separate-repos.md §1.2).
-- The modules moved out of the std library (`lib/Hdl` -> `hdl/src/Hdl`) with no import
-- change: they are still `Hdl.*`, and the std primitives they import (`BitVec`, `Vec`,
-- `Trace`, `Optic`, `Deriving`, `IO`, `Text`, `Std`) come from the toolchain's `lib/`,
-- not from a root of this package.
--
--   grail build                 check the library in src/
--   grail build hdl             just the library
--   grail test                  every example, its messages against examples/NAME.expected
--
-- Both roots are relative to this file's directory (`src` and `examples`), and the std
-- comes from the toolchain that runs grail, so a copy of `hdl/` builds and tests on its
-- own: `scripts/check-standalone.sh` proves it, and CI reads the package through
-- `HDL_ROOT` (default `hdl`). The dependency is one-way (`hdl` -> the std `lib/`);
-- `scripts/check-boundaries.py` enforces it.
--
-- `scripts/gen-uart-temporal.py` regenerates the marked case analyses inside
-- `examples/hdl-uart-temporal.wiz`.
def package : Package := Package.new "hdl"
  |> Package.version "0.1.0"
  |> Package.toolchain ">=0.1.0 <0.3.0"
  |> Package.lib "hdl" "src"
  |> Package.tests "examples" "examples"
